    76	    "§6930. Effective date (a) Preliminary notification Not later than ninety days after "
    77	    "promulgation of regulations under section 6921 of this title identifying by its "
    78	    "characteristics or listing any substance as hazardous waste subject to this subchapter, any "
    79	    "person generating or transporting such substance or owning or operating a facility for "
    80	    "treatment, storage, or disposal of such substance shall file with the Administrator (or with "
    81	    "States having authorized hazardous waste permit programs under section 6926 of this title) a "
    82	    "notification stating the location and general description of such activity and the "
    83	    "identified or listed hazardous wastes handled by such person. Not later than fifteen months "
    84	    "after November 8, 1984— (1) the owner or operator of any facility which produces a fuel (A) "
    85	    "from any hazardous waste identified or listed under section 6921 of this title, (B) from "
    86	    "such hazardous waste identified or listed under section 6921 of this title and any other "
    87	    "material, (C) from used oil, or (D) from used oil and any other material; (2) the owner or "
    88	    "operator of any facility (other than a single- or two-family residence) which burns for "
    89	    "purposes of energy recovery any fuel produced as provided in paragraph (1) or any fuel which "
    90	    "otherwise contains used oil or any hazardous waste identified or listed under section 6921 "
    91	    "of this title; and (3) any person who distributes or markets any fuel which is produced as "
    92	    "provided in paragraph (1) or any fuel which otherwise contains used oil or any hazardous "
    93	    "waste identified or listed under section 6921 of this title 1 shall file with the "
    94	    "Administrator (and with the State in the case of a State with an authorized hazardous waste "
    95	    "program) a notification stating the location and general description of the facility, "
    96	    "together with a description of the identified or listed hazardous waste involved and, in the "
    97	    "case of a facility referred to in paragraph (1) or (2), a description of the production or "
    98	    "energy recovery activity carried out at the facility and such other information as the "
    99	    "Administrator deems necessary. For purposes of the preceding provisions, the term \"hazardous "
   100	    "waste listed under section 6921 of this title\" also includes any commercial chemical product "
   101	    "which is listed under section 6921 of this title and which, in lieu of its original intended "
   102	    "use, is (i) produced for use as (or as a component of) a fuel, (ii) distributed for use as a "
