   151	    "§60101. Boarding arriving vessels before inspection (a) Regulations .—The Secretary of "
   152	    "Homeland Security shall prescribe and enforce regulations on the boarding of a vessel "
   153	    "arriving at a port of the United States before the vessel has been inspected and secured. "
   154	    "(b) Criminal Penalty .—A person violating a regulation prescribed under this section shall "
   155	    "be fined under title 18, imprisoned for not more than 6 months, or both. (c) Relationship to "
   156	    "Other law .—This section shall be construed as supplementary to section 2279 of title 18. "
   157	    "(Pub. L. 109–304, §9(b), Oct. 6, 2006, 120 Stat. 1674.) Historical and Revision Notes "
   158	    "Revised Section Source (U.S. Code) Source (Statutes at Large) 60101 46 App.:163. Mar. 31, "
   159	    "1900, ch. 120, §§1–3, 31 Stat. 58. In subsection (a), the Secretary of Homeland Security is "
   160	    "substituted for the Commissioner of Customs because the functions of the Customs Service and "
